name c01m04-silkworm-jungle
timeout 700
time 1996-03-21T01:00:00Z

# F-22 LIGHTNING II (NovaLogic 1996), CAMPAIGN ONE, SORTIE 1.4 OF 8 — "SILKWORM JUNGLE".
# Spec: mods/f22/doc/campaign.md 2. Geometry: mods/f22/doc/terrain.md 3. Substitutions:
# mods/f22/doc/substitutions.md. The five campaign-wide disclosures: c01m01-snake-eyes.fbm.
#
# THE TASK [TXT]: intercept three An-225 carrying Silkworm missiles out of Kunming. Flight group
# `Alpha`, briefed 60 NM NNE; measured 56.5 NM on bearing 43.0 deg [ORF] — the campaign's second worst
# briefing bearing (+20.5 deg off the stated octant).
#
# SUBSTITUTIONS IN THIS FILE
#   An-225 Cossack -> `kc135` (KC-135R), and it is the catalogue's LARGE FOUR-ENGINE JET rather than
#     its `an26`. What decides against a transport in this tree is span (the eye resolves on presented
#     extent), speed and ceiling, and on all three the C-135 is the nearer row: span 39.88 m against
#     the An-225's 88.4 m and the An-26's 29.3 m; cruise 237 m/s against ~222 m/s and 122 m/s. The
#     error is still large and it runs AGAINST the mission: the substitute is HALF the wingspan, so
#     visual acquisition happens later than it would against the real aircraft. It is a tanker row
#     standing in for a freighter; nothing about it carries or drops anything, and the Silkworms it is
#     supposed to be delivering exist only in the briefing.
#   MiG-27 escort -> `mig23`, as everywhere in this campaign.
#
# "BEFORE THEY LEAVE THE BOX" IS A DECLARED SPAN, AND THAT IS THE ONE THING THIS SORTIE PROVES ABOUT
# THE FORMAT. campaign.md's reading rule for 1.4 is a verdict against a clock, and `until <s>`
# (doc/missions/verdict.md, "the seventh thing in the vocabulary") is exactly that: the objective's
# state is FROZEN at the declared instant. THE NUMBER IS DERIVED, not chosen:
#   route      alpha point -> bearing 223 deg, 130.0 km, which lands on 18.664 N / 100.185 E — the
#              SOUTH-WEST CORNER of sortie 1.4's own bounding box (terrain.md 3: min_lat 18.664,
#              min_lon 100.172). That is what "leaves the box" means, spelled as a waypoint.
#   speed      `kc135`'s catalogue cruise, 237.0 m/s (core/FBAircraft.h, kKc135)
#   until      130 000 / 237.0 = 548.5 s -> `until 548`, the last whole second still inside the box.
# A kill at t = 549 is therefore NOT a kill for this mission's purposes, and the objective says so
# instead of a header asking a reader to check a timestamp.
#
# WHY THE ESCORT'S KILL SITS ON THE WINGMAN. campaign.md: "the MiG-27 escort is a target of
# opportunity and killing it proves nothing". But an aircraft that dies without being anybody's
# declared objective ends the run CRASH/exit 2 (doc/missions/verdict.md, the combination rule), which
# would make an irrelevant kill decide the mission. The declaration is therefore SPLIT: `s4lead`
# carries the three transports and nothing else, `s4two` carries the escort. The escort's death is
# then covered — the run stays legible — and it cannot enter the sortie's verdict, because the
# sortie's verdict is `s4lead`'s UNIT_RESULT. This device is used in 1.4, 1.6 and 1.8.
#
# READING RULE (binding). The verdict is `s4lead`'s UNIT_RESULT.
#   SUCCESS/exit 0 = all three `until 548` kills met and Storm Leader combat-effective at the end.
#   Two of three is a MISSION LOSS and reads as TIMEOUT/exit 3 with the unmet kill named in the
#   `mission OBJECTIVE` vector — the transport that got through is the one to report.
#   `s4two`'s result is NOT the mission's under any outcome, and a run in which the escort survives
#   while all three transports die is a full success of this sortie.
#   exit 2 = a HOSTILE aircraft died that nobody declared, or an airframe departed controlled flight
#   with nobody having shot it. It is an ENGINE finding either way. It is NOT what a friendly loss
#   looks like: a friendly with `survive` fails DECISIVELY, which ends the run before its wreck can
#   reach the ground, and that reads exit 1 (measured four times over in this campaign).

# MEASURED (exit 0): ALL THREE, AND WELL INSIDE THE WINDOW.
#   t = 95.2 / 95.4 s   `s4an1` and `s4an2` combat-ineffective
#   t = 242.0 s         `s4an3`; t = 243.7 s the escort
#   verdict             `s4lead` SUCCESS, all three `until 548` kills met with 306 s to spare;
#                       `s4two` SUCCESS. Run ends t = 329.3 s
#   THE WINDOW DID NOT BIND on this run and was not meant to. What it does is make the condition
#   machine-checkable: a kill at t = 549 would have read `state=unmet` with the object DESTROYED.

unit s4lead
  module f16
  team friendly
  flight storm4 1
  spawn 19.15691 100.67021 8000 43.0 480      # 55 km down-track of the Alpha point, at their altitude
  set gear up
  set fuel_int_pct 100
  set datalink on
  set fcr_mode crm
  set fcr_range_nm 40
  set rwr on
  set store 1 aim9
  set store 2 aim120
  set store 3 aim120
  set store 7 aim120
  set store 8 aim120
  set store 9 aim9
  set gun_rounds 480
  set cmds_mode auto
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 60
  set cmds_flare 60
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task intercept
  wp 19.51825 101.02731 8000 480              # the Alpha point [ORF] 56.5 NM / 43.0 deg from Tyler
  objective kill unit s4an1 until 548
  objective kill unit s4an2 until 548
  objective kill unit s4an3 until 548
  objective survive

unit s4two
  module f16
  team friendly
  flight storm4 2
  spawn 19.14772 100.68064 8000 43.0 480      # 1.5 km across track from the leader
  set gear up
  set fuel_int_pct 100
  set datalink on
  set fcr_mode crm
  set fcr_range_nm 40
  set rwr on
  set store 1 aim9
  set store 2 aim120
  set store 3 aim120
  set store 7 aim120
  set store 8 aim120
  set store 9 aim9
  set gun_rounds 480
  set cmds_mode auto
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 60
  set cmds_flare 60
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task intercept
  wp 19.51825 101.02731 8000 480
  objective kill unit s4esc
  objective survive

unit s4an1
  module kc135
  team hostile
  spawn 19.51825 101.02731 8000 223.0 460     # AT the Alpha point, outbound on 223 deg
  wp 18.66418 100.18452 8000 460              # the box's south-west corner, 130.0 km away

unit s4an2
  module kc135
  team hostile
  spawn 19.53051 101.01337 8000 223.0 460     # 2 km abeam
  wp 18.66418 100.18452 8000 460

unit s4an3
  module kc135
  team hostile
  spawn 19.54276 100.99943 8000 223.0 460     # 4 km abeam
  wp 18.66418 100.18452 8000 460

unit s4esc
  module mig23
  team hostile
  spawn 19.55767 101.06632 8000 223.0 450     # 6 km behind the transports, same track
  set gear up
  set task intercept
  set brief_gci 223 60 8000
  set store 1 r24r
  set store 2 r24r
  set brief_master_arm arm
  wp 18.66418 100.18452 8000 450
  objective survive
